## Final Judgement
### Summary of Key Insights
The retrieved evidence clearly demonstrates that the portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah at Aligarh Muslim University (AMU) was installed in 1938, when Jinnah was granted life membership of the student union. This installation occurred decades before Maskoor Usmani—who served as the AMU Students' Union President in 2017 and was later positioned as a Congress party candidate in 2020—was even born. Official university records, statements from AMU spokespersons, and independent fact-checks confirm that the portrait has been a historical fixture of the university since 1938, and there is absolutely no evidence linking Usmani to its installation. The allegation originated from a false news broadcast by the channel *AajTak* in October 2020, which Usmani subsequently denounced as a lie in a complaint to the Election Commission. Because the evidence is definitive and leaves no room for ambiguity, no further investigation is required.

### Conclusion
Based on the verified evidence, the claim that Maskoor Usmani installed Jinnah's portrait at AMU is completely false. The portrait was already hanging in the university's student union hall nearly eighty years before Usmani was elected as the student union president, making the allegation chronologically and physically impossible. Therefore, the final decision is that the claim is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The allegation that Maskoor Usmani installed Muhammad Ali Jinnah's portrait at Aligarh Muslim University (AMU) is completely false. Historical records and university spokespersons confirm that the portrait has been hanging in the student union hall since [1938](https://frontline.thehindu.com/the-nation/jaundiced-perspective/article10108356.ece), when Jinnah was granted life membership—decades before Usmani was even born. [Aligarh Muslim University](https://thewire.in/communalism/jinnah-portrait-at-aligarh-muslim-university-sparks-row) clarified that displaying photographs of all life members is a traditional practice, and there is no evidence linking Usmani to its installation. The false claim originated from an [AajTak](https://www.thequint.com/news/webqoof/aajtaks-claim-that-maskoor-usmani-hung-jinnah-portrait-at-amu-is-false) news broadcast in October 2020, which Usmani, who served as the AMU Students' Union President in 2017, subsequently denounced in a complaint to the Election Commission.